#
# This is a comprehensive .gitignore for a React project.
# It ignores dependencies, build outputs, log files,
# environment variables, and common IDE editor folders.

### React / Node ###

# Dependencies
# Never commit node_modules. This directory is regenerated on `npm install`.
/node_modules

# Production builds
# This folder contains the optimized, bundled code for deployment.
/build
/dist
/out

# NPM / Yarn debug logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Environment variables
# These files often contain sensitive API keys and secrets.
# Commit the .env.example file as a template for other developers.
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
.env.*.local

# Coverage reports
# Generated by testing tools like Jest.
/coverage

# Optional cache folders
.npm
.yarn-cache

---

### IDE & Editor Folders ###

# IntelliJ IDEA / WebStorm / JetBrains
# User-specific settings, caches, and run configurations.
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# Visual Studio Code
# User-specific settings, launch configurations, and workspace history.
.vscode/
# Note: Some teams choose to commit `.vscode/settings.json` if it
# contains project-specific formatting rules (e.g., for Prettier).
# To do that, add `!.vscode/settings.json` on a new line.

# Other Editors
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db